{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134828-story-hooks-for-kids","id":1134828,"title":"Story Hooks for Kids","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T07:31:59-07:00","id":1134828,"title":"Story Hooks for Kids","content":"I'm planning to start a game with my two oldest kids (11 And 7), and I'm looking for ideas for PGish stories. They want to play a brother and sister who get mixed up in spooky mysteries. Just looking for suggestions to help get the mental wheels turning. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T07:47:44-07:00","id":1134832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134828-story-hooks-for-kids#post1134828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm planning to start a game with my two oldest kids (11 And 7), and I'm looking for ideas for PGish stories. They want to play a brother and sister who get mixed up in spooky mysteries. Just looking for suggestions to help get the mental wheels turning. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you list what themes you want to explore, and how severe you want things to get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-28-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T08:01:05-07:00","id":1134837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134828-story-hooks-for-kids?p=1134832#post1134832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can you list what themes you want to explore, and how severe your want thing to get?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah, kids stuff can be pretty dark: Harry Potter, Goosebumps, Roald Dahl, Edward Gorey, you name it. Kids can take a lot as long as it comes with a gruesomely funny or happy ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T08:30:24-07:00","id":1134843,"title":"","content":"Also the setting you have in mind can be useful to know. Some plot hooks are kinda tied to certain environments, so knowing might help us help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:58:54-07:00","id":1134879,"title":"","content":"When the sun goes down every pet in the neighborhood takes off into the dark, those locked inside stand waiting beside the door not whining, just waiting. When the sun returns so do the pets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T03:03:26-07:00","id":1135112,"title":"","content":"Goosebumps has some pretty cool ideas for you for sure.<br /> <br /> Have something weird happen to a friend of the siblings e.g. Sudden extreme fur growth Or An imagined Friend From Their Past Come To Live As An invisible troublemaker.<br /> Make things disappear it by bit or even all at once. e.g. all mirrors or silver Ware, so they organize a stake out to find the culprit (maybe tiny fae?).<br /> Have the local museum get a special delivery/exhibition that goes wonky as their exhibit A Starts running around (mummies and cavemen are all - time favorites for this). Maybe the school pushed harder on their tests, and Children who fail the New monthly special test are sent to the Principal, to be a) never seen again and even forgotten by the adults b) Become Model Children - obedient, always Clean And proper, diligent, unimaginative, lifeless.<br /> Mirrors are now a pathway Network that can be used by Children a la Jonathan strange. What seemed perfectly safe and fun at first turns more and more into stranger things upsidedown, and Children start to go missing - even after no one uses the mirrorpathways anymore. Were they a trap? Was there something coming for them from the other side?<br /> <br /> Any &quot;adults dont get it/dont see it&quot; e.g. due to magic makes their actions more impactful. Adults are useless is a common trope for a reason.<br /> <br /> You could also have them stumble upon a magic book and Release an ancient evil/curse one of them. Or have someone from their class do it and them clean up the mess (e.g curse of monsters coming for that classmate Whenever They fall asleep - now they need to break the curse, and fast! There is only so much bonus the magic option known as coffee can provide to the Stay awake roll...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-29-2017, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:46:41-07:00","id":1135331,"title":"","content":"To go a step further than Wormwood, &quot;Kill the parents&quot; is a foundational piece of child story writing. You don't need to literally kill them, but for child characters to have meaningful agency it's best to remove parents and other adult authority figures from the equation early on. The easiest thing to do would be to make this the crux of the story. Something kidnaps, kills, curses, or otherwise incapacitates the parents and the children have to figure out a way to stop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T01:38:05-07:00","id":1135370,"title":"","content":"You can keep adults from getting involved by just falling back on the clich\u00e9 &quot;That's nice dear. He has such a vivid imagination.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bOr use isolation, a horror story classic, by placing the story in a place where the kids don't have any adults they think they can trust, summer camp for example. I will say that if you want to keep it PG enough for a 7 year old I wouldn't go too dark.<br /> <br /> \u200bBack to the OP; there is a new kid at the playground and they really like him but no one knows where he lives. They ask him but when they go to the address given they find a house that has been empty for years, perhaps due to a fire or maybe the people who lived there just disappeared.<br /> <br /> \u200bThey find a stray animal and because mom and dad won't let them have a pet they keep it hidden. It's a strange little creature though, not like any cat or dog they've ever seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T04:32:15-07:00","id":1135390,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I have an idea for an innocents chronicle that I have been playing around with. The core principle could easily be turned into a story for kids, though I only have experience roleplaying with kids around age 10-14, so Im by no means an expert:<br /> <br /> The parents are in a car crash. They will live, but they are hospitalized for a long time (Nevermind that they are hospitalized for months, thats the sort of thing thats pretty easy to buy into)... So the players are sent to live with their uncle for a while, while the parents make their full recovery. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now the thing about this uncle is that he is the classic enigmatic old coot, also, he is secretly a mage. He is by no means a people person, he is a grumpy solitare that takes no pleasure in taking care of relatives he havent seen in years. Whats more important, he happens to know just how deep the rabbits hole is around his home. In my concept, the small town he lives in is on top of a huge Iris into the hedge (Though it could be any supernatural force... A gate to Shadow is a good alternative by my book).. So the uncle is not fond of having children present in what is basicly a hotspot for supernatural dangers. <br /> <br /> Naturally the uncle aint around much, seeing as he is secretly out acting as a protector of the city, while doing everything in his power to keep the players from getting entangled in his &quot;Grown up buisness&quot; <br /> <br /> Then all you need to do is have the players stumble upon the supernatural.. Maybe they get in trouble over at school, and overhear that the principle conspireing to get the uncle killed or taking over the town, you know, because he is a true fae, or spirit ridden or whatever suits your tastes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the smart thing to do is not to get too dark at first, in the setup I have been chewing on, the kids are not in any immidiate danger. They havent lost anyone dear to them. And if they get in over their heads, they might get rescued by the uncle in disguise. <br /> <br /> That way you can adjust the plot and darkness according to how your players respond, if they dig into the plot full on, figuring its up to them, then you can amp up the tension a bit, when the uncle gets wounded or disappears. If they instead seem uneasy, and seek constant comfort by avoiding the plot or trying to get adult help. Then you can use the uncle as a safety net: he reveals that the monsters are real, but for one contrived reason or the other, he needs the kids help in the extend you deem appropiate. Could be anything from &quot;Spy on the principal&quot; to &quot;Almost get kidnapped so he can lure the monster out.&quot; <br /> <br /> Some great inspiration if you want to share some time watching tv or reading stories with the kids, to get a feel for what they are interested in could be: <br /> Brothers Grimm stories. <br /> Over the Guarden wall <br /> Gravity falls<br /> <br /> So yeah, main thing is figuring what they want to play, and how dark it should get... No idea if this helps, but best of luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:21:21-07:00","id":1135417,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I like the Summer Camp and strange uncle ideas!<br /> <br /> Simplest way to take all adults out and give a plot hook would be to just make all adults disappear. Now the Children have to Find out what happened, deal with however you decide to get them back, take care of each other in slowly failing infrastructure and possibly have to deal with those Kids that oppose the adults' return efforts. Then, those that have their (age of your choosing, let's go with 12) th birthday Suddenly vanish at midnight, leaving just empty clothes behind ...<br /> <br /> Reasons can be anything from Spirits of Childhood, mage spell going wonky, a fae Whisking people away to create his own neverneverland, some sort of magic artifact (possible tie-in with the aforementioned Museum exhibition idea) etc etc. I am sure you are able to find something to use. Although I am partial to Ghosts/Spirits, Mages or Fae for kid stories, myself. Nice, rich, suitably Creepy symbolic value, without going overboard. Making vampire or werewolves fitting might be a tad bit harder But is Certainly possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:24:03-07:00","id":1135438,"title":"","content":"Rather than full-blown werewolves you could have them befriend a wolf-blooded kid. Maybe one with the tell that lets them take urhan form. <br /> <br /> Maybe have a plot where the wolf-skin that lets them do that gets stolen or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:00:28-07:00","id":1135449,"title":"","content":"There's an unpopular kid at school who has become kind of a bully magnet. He disappears into the nurse's/principal's office or goes home each time. It takes some months before your characters realize he's never exhibited any bruises or broken bones the next day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:23:58-07:00","id":1135480,"title":"","content":"School bully turns out to be a literal beast (though perhaps not a Beast)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:05:08-07:00","id":1135489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134828-story-hooks-for-kids?p=1135480#post1135480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">School bully turns out to be a literal beast (though perhaps not a Beast)</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are perfect for innocents games in my opinion, but as for hooks,<br /> <br /> family curses don't have to spare the children...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:58:29-07:00","id":1135510,"title":"","content":"You could have an eternally-young vampire that causes trouble with his nightly visits, and his growing need for blood.<br /> A promethean made from a young kid, might be why he's bullied.<br /> A beast teacher (anakim tyrant or the Namtaru tyrant example from the core, maybe?) Who Swings between really nice and totally mean and scary for no observable reason. Or who rules his class with an Iron fist, makes them memorize a lot of Information and who tries to teach them &quot;Knowledge is power that can keep you alive&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can also make use of the good old ghosthouse plot, via a Ball landing on the Front lawn, or a test of courage. Up to you whether it is ghosts, spirits, prommies-in-hiding or something else entirely. Can be any type of scary place, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T22:45:27-07:00","id":1135679,"title":"","content":"A children's story classic is for the kids to set out to prove that some legendary creature is real, in spite of the disbelief of adults. Usually this involves old buildings, dark forests or mountain lakes. Nothing too far from home though.<br /> \u200bYou could also go Jumanji, with the kids playing a game of fantasy that proves all too real and the only way to escape is to finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:48:49-07:00","id":1135858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134828-story-hooks-for-kids?p=1135679#post1135679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A children's story classic is for the kids to set out to prove that some legendary creature is real, in spite of the disbelief of adults. Usually this involves old buildings, dark forests or mountain lakes. Nothing too far from home though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me think of the urban legends on Hey Arnold, in fact, having some kid who is an expert on local urban legends act as a GM mouthpiece when needed isn't that bad an idea.<br /> <br /> Also, an item found during the initial adventure turns out to be key to a larger mystery, ala gravity falls (the journal) or Scooby Doo mystery incorporated (the locket)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:47:44-07:00","id":1149099,"title":"","content":"*bump*<br /> Curious to hear if something came out of it, and if so, how it went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}